{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL stock schema as the branch_stock database on node1 with the supplied stock and supplier-cost records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied SQL defines both required tables and four records. Final inspection on node1 shows branch_stock containing stock values LABELS:18 and PAPER:40 and supplier costs LABELS:1.75 and PAPER:3.25; PostgreSQL is active, enabled, and listening on node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1202bb51c1ed4924","cmd-b83cd648e12048f7","cmd-aaadd076d5ac46eb","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update only stock quantities, without schema-change or supplier_cost access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote tests from node2 show stock_app reading stock and successfully updating quantity inside a rolled-back transaction. Supplier-cost reads, schema creation, SKU updates, inserts, and deletes were denied. Final privilege inspection confirms SELECT on stock, UPDATE only on quantity, and no supplier_costs SELECT or schema CREATE privilege.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8cfe60478f64a47","cmd-477b7a9037ad4f6d","cmd-9e9589f7f8c84212","cmd-396051e9b7f04980","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The auditor remotely read both tables. Attempts to update either table and create schema objects were denied, while final effective-privilege checks show SELECT access to both tables and no stock UPDATE or schema CREATE privilege.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0ca4e124aaca4351","cmd-5de6a878a1b0491f","cmd-396051e9b7f04980","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has distinct per-role pgpass credentials in separate root-owned mode-0600 files under a mode-0700 directory. Distinctness and successful authentication as each role were directly tested before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9aeaac8f32aa4abe","cmd-7e02b8e8d3ed448d","cmd-396051e9b7f04980","cmd-2cc6d150b4fd4d94"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the supplied records in /srv/legacy2/database-reader-writer-roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sole baseline file, stock.sql, retained the baseline SHA-256 value 7934fb042f67368428ae2fcf771fef48d1e6154f8d0d1e6b1c9d144c7d5622ea on both nodes through final verification and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-b83cd648e12048f7","cmd-396051e9b7f04980","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6","cmd-2cc6d150b4fd4d94"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. PostgreSQL 16.15 packages came from the native RHEL repositories and remained healthy after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d8f7b93ef25341e0","cmd-6e3903c39edd4567","cmd-df26aaff490343f1","cmd-37042c35f08f4232","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6","cmd-2cc6d150b4fd4d94","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Operational state is clean: final snapshots show no failed services or package-health problems, PostgreSQL is narrowly bound to node1's managed address, and temporary test outputs are absent. One unnecessary bounded mutation occurred: cmd-7977f72041a8400e created /etc/branch_stock and an empty credential_salt before failing because openssl was unavailable. It was fully reverted by cmd-2b8c849869ad4647 before the working credential setup. No other unnecessary mutations are evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7977f72041a8400e","cmd-2b8c849869ad4647","cmd-d5556fecd7c047f6","cmd-2cc6d150b4fd4d94","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol is complete on both managed nodes: healthy pre-restart states and boot identities were captured, each restart was acknowledged, different post-restart identities were observed, and services, data, credentials, and access controls recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["Evidence is captured and bounded rather than a live-system inspection.","The role-creation command emitted a harmless malformed psql meta-command error, but subsequent direct database, privilege, authentication, data, and restart-recovery observations coherently establish the intended final state."]}
